                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Could we please do something better than \"Name2\"?  You wouldn't name a variable or child \"Name2\" so why would we name a JSON key that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry if I get your question inaccurately,\nCan you please give me your inputs in below context:\n```\n        {\n            \"Address\": \"0x76\",\n            \"Bus\": \"7\",\n            \"Name\": \"BME280 Temp Sensor 1\",\n            \"Name1\": \"BME280 Pressure Sensor 1\",\n            \"Name2\": \"BME280 Humidity Sensor 1\",\n            \"Type\": \"BME280\"\n        }\n```\nThe current patch is aligned with the approach above.\n\nAre you suggesting to use something differently? like changing the key to something more intuitive ?\nPlease let me know your POV.\nThanks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Changing the key to something more intuitive.\n\nIs this a case where BME280 only uses name1 / name2, or is this a case where \"name1\" is always used as a pressure sensor across all devices and \"name2\" is always a humidity sensor?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Seems like this is across multiple device types.  So can we change the key to something more intuitive?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please suggest what key would work for Pressure & Humidity ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "\"NamePressure\"?  Anything is better than \"Name1\", right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure.\nI'll keep it in below way:\n\nNamePressure -> For Pressure sensor\nNameHumidity -> For Humidity sensor\n\nWhat about Temperature sensor ?\nCurrently key used is Name\nShould I update it as well ? Something like NameTemperature ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
